  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A parallel plate capacitor consists of two plates separated by <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"5.0\\ \\text{mm}\"></span> and charged to a potential difference of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"200.0\\ \\text{V}\"></span>. A proton (<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"q = 1.60 \\times 10^{-19}\\ \\text{C}\"></span>, <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"m = 1.67 \\times 10^{-27}\\ \\text{kg}\"></span>) is released from rest near the positive plate and moves toward the negative plate.</p><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"a\"><p><strong>a</strong> Calculate the electric field strength between the plates. [2]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"b\"><p><strong>b</strong> Determine the force acting on the proton. [1]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"c\"><p><strong>c</strong> Calculate the acceleration of the proton. [1]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"d\"><p><strong>d</strong> Determine the kinetic energy gained by the proton when it reaches the negative plate. [2]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"e\"><p><strong>e</strong> Calculate the final speed of the proton. [2]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"f\"><p><strong>f</strong> Explain why the motion of the proton in the capacitor is similar to free fall near Earth’s surface. [1]</p></section>"
